<title>NETHERLANDS: VAN LANSCHOT CUTS IHC TO MARKET PERFORMER.</title>
<headline>VAN LANSCHOT CUTS IHC TO MARKET PERFORMER.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of company update.</p>
<p>Company---------Sector---------Price---Broker-------------</p>
<p>IHC Caland    Offshore tech    112.00  Van Lanschot</p>
<p>COMMENT: Market performer (from outperform). 1996</p>
<p>preliminary profit of 93 million guilders (3.69 per share)</p>
<p>leaves something to be desired. 1997 outlook most likely to be</p>
<p>upgraded in April and again in August. Stock more than well</p>
<p>valued at close to 25 times earnings, given 16 pct and 17 pct</p>
<p>growth rate for '97 and '98. Fundamentals still good.</p>
<p>    Estimates (Dfl):   EPS	 P/E     Dividend</p>
<p>    1995 (actual)	3.17	35.4    1.60</p>
<p>    1996		   3.69	30.3    1.85</p>
<p>    1997		   4.30	26.0    2.15</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
